-- title:
--   Automorphisms act on m-th roots of unity as Frobenius powers
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime number and let $m$ be a natural number with $q \nmid m$. Let $\sigma$ be an automorphism of the field `PadicAlgCl q`, an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_q$, as a $\mathbb{Q}_q$-algebra. The assertion is that there exists a natural number $k$ such that for every $x \in$ `PadicAlgCl q` with $x^m = 1$ one has $\sigma(x) = x^{q^k}$. Thus a single exponent $k$, depending on $\sigma$ (and on $q$ and $m$) but not on $x$, serves simultaneously for all $m$-th roots of unity in the algebraic closure: on the group $\mu_m$ the automorphism $\sigma$ coincides with the $k$-th power of the map $x \mapsto x^q$. Note that $k$ is only asserted to exist as a natural number, and no claim is made about its uniqueness, its size, or about $\sigma$ outside $\mu_m$; the hypothesis $q \nmid m$ forces $m > 0$, so the case $m = 0$ is excluded.
--
--   This is the classical statement that $\mathbb{Q}_q(\mu_m)/\mathbb{Q}_q$ is unramified for $q \nmid m$ with Galois group generated by the arithmetic Frobenius $x \mapsto x^q$, in the form: every $\mathbb{Q}_q$-automorphism of the algebraic closure acts on $\mu_m$ as a power of Frobenius. It is used in the construction and classification of unramified characters and of étale algebras over $\mathbb{Z}_q$, by [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.inflate_sub_unitsInflate2_carryFun_mem_levelCoboundaries2`](thm.html#NumberField.PlaceDecomp.inflate_sub_unitsInflate2_carryFun_mem_levelCoboundaries2), [`PadicAlgCl.exists_unramified_level_char_of_sq_sub_one_mem_span_socle`](thm.html#PadicAlgCl.exists_unramified_level_char_of_sq_sub_one_mem_span_socle) and [`PadicInt.exists_etale_algebra_algHom_equiv_zmod`](thm.html#PadicInt.exists_etale_algebra_algHom_equiv_zmod).
